, CA, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Mischler G", "lastName": "Mischler", "firstName": "Gavin", "initials": "G", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4776-3518"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Mortimer B. Zuckerman Mind Brain Behavior Institute, Columbia University, New York, NY, USA."}, {"affiliation": "Department of Electrical Engineering, Columbia University, New York, NY, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Mesgarani N", "lastName": "Mesgarani", "firstName": "Nima", "initials": "N", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-2987-759X"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Mortimer B. Zuckerman Mind Brain Behavior Institute, Columbia University, New York, NY, USA."}, {"affiliation": "Department of Electrical Engineering, Columbia University, New York, NY, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Welkenhuysen M", "lastName": "Welkenhuysen", "firstName": "Marleen", "initials": "M", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-6729-9391"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "IMEC, Leuven, Belgium."}]}}, {"fullName": "Dutta B", "lastName": "Dutta", "firstName": "Barundeb", "initials": "B", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4781-9630"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "IMEC, Leuven, Belgium."}]}}, {"fullName": "Chang EF", "lastName": "Chang", "firstName": "Edward F", "initials": "EF", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-2480-4700"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Neurological Surgery, University of California, San Francisco, San Francisco, CA, USA. edward.chang@ucsf.edu."}, {"affiliation": "Weill Institute for Neurosciences, University of California, San Francisco, San Francisco, CA, USA. edward.chang@ucsf.edu."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-6729-9391"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-0517-2296"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-2987-759X"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-8259-8688"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-8530-880X"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-2480-4700"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4776-3518"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4781-9630"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "7999", "volume": "626", "journalIssueId": 3715004, "dateOfPublication": "2024 Feb", "monthOfPublication": 2, "yearOfPublication": 2024, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Nature", "title": "Nature", "essn": "1476-4687", "issn": "0028-0836", "nlmid": "0410462", "isoabbreviation": "Nature"}, "printPublicationDate": "2024-02-01"}, "pubYear": "2024", "pageInfo": "593-602", "abstractText": "Understanding the neural basis of speech perception requires that we study the human brain both at the scale of the fundamental computational unit of neurons and in their organization across the depth of cortex. Here we used high-density Neuropixels arrays<sup>1-3</sup> to record from 685 neurons across cortical layers at nine sites in a high-level auditory region that is critical for speech, the superior temporal gyrus<sup>4,5</sup>, while participants listened to spoken sentences. Single neurons encoded a wide range of speech sound cues, including features of consonants and vowels, relative vocal pitch, onsets, amplitude envelope and sequence statistics. Neurons at each cross-laminar recording exhibited dominant tuning to a primary speech feature while also containing a substantial proportion of neurons that encoded other features contributing to heterogeneous selectivity. Spatially, neurons at similar cortical depths tended to encode similar speech features. Activity across all cortical layers was predictive of high-frequency field potentials (electrocorticography), providing a neuronal origin for macroelectrode recordings from the cortical surface. Together, these results establish single-neuron tuning across the cortical laminae as an important dimension of speech encoding in human superior temporal gyrus.", "affiliation": "Department of Neurological Surgery, University of California, San Francisco, San Francisco, CA, USA.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["research-article", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NINDS NIH HHS", "acronym": "NS", "grantId": "R25 NS070680", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIDCD NIH HHS", "acronym": "DC", "grantId": "R01 DC014279", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIDCD NIH HHS", "acronym": "DC", "grantId": "R01 DC012379", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIDCD NIH HHS", "acronym": "DC", "grantId": "R01 DC018805", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NINDS NIH HHS", "acronym": "NS", "grantId": "UE5 NS070680", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Temporal Lobe", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "CY", "qualifierName": "cytology"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "PH", "qualifierName": "physiology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Auditory Cortex", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "CY", "qualifierName": "cytology"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "PH", "qualifierName": "physiology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Neurons", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "PH", "qualifierName": "physiology"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Acoustic Stimulation"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Electrodes"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Speech"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Cues"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Speech Perception", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQual